Z||000006||Smoooooth GT||07-19-2001||09:11 AM||||GREAT job Aus....  How many Fiero's are in Australia??  My mom visited Melbourne last year and said that she saw around 10 or so in the 3 week's she was there...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG">   <BR>  with a 100-125HP shot of NOS...||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||07-19-2001||09:26 AM||||Well smooth the number is debatable. I have one guy who reckons 300 to 400. I think he is full of it. On the other hand I know Ponti-World is Australias major Pontiac spare parts supplier and Dave the owner is president of the Pontiac Car Club of Australia, and a personal friend of mine. <P>Between his database, ads for sale in magazines and who we know between us we reckon about 70 to 100. NSW has not many. QLD has most of the Fieros. VIC has more than I thought if she seen 10 of them and the other states don't have a lot at all.<P>I now know of 3 t-topped cars. Mine, another 86 GT fastback and an 88 Formula sitting in holding for when I want it. The Formula is a factory t-topped car. It is a steal too at $6000 AUS and already RHD. Has no interior and is a bit rough but a RHD conversion is $5000 alone. Kind of the perfect project for my radical Fiero custom I want.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
